{"question_id": "36", "question": "Under whose administration does the school with the highest number of test takers whose total SAT Scores are greater or equal to 1500 belong to? Indicate his or her full name.", "evidence": "full name means first name, last name; There are at most 3 administrators for each school; SAT Scores are greater or equal to 1500 refers to NumGE1500", "schema": "CREATE TABLE frpm\n(\n    CDSCode                                       TEXT not null\n        primary key,\n    `Academic Year`                               TEXT  null,\n    `County Code`                                 TEXT  null,\n    `District Code`                               INTEGER         null,\n    `School Code`                                 TEXT  null,\n    `County Name`                                 TEXT null,\n    `District Name`                               TEXT null,\n    `School Name`                                 TEXT null,\n    `District Type`                               TEXT null,\n    `School Type`                                 TEXT null,\n    `Educational Option Type`                     TEXT null,\n    `NSLP Provision Status`                       TEXT null,\n    `Charter School (Y/N)`                        INTEGER    null,\n    `Charter School Number`                       TEXT  null,\n    `Charter Funding Type`                        TEXT null,\n    IRC                                           INTEGER    null,\n    `Low Grade`                                   TEXT  null,\n    `High Grade`                                  TEXT null,\n    `Enrollment (K-12)`                           REAL      null,\n    `Free Meal Count (K-12)`                      REAL       null,\n    `Percent (%) Eligible Free (K-12)`            REAL       null,\n    `FRPM Count (K-12)`                           REAL       null,\n    `Percent (%) Eligible FRPM (K-12)`            REAL       null,\n    `Enrollment (Ages 5-17)`                      REAL       null,\n    `Free Meal Count (Ages 5-17)`                 REAL       null,\n    `Percent (%) Eligible Free (Ages 5-17)`       REAL       null,\n    `FRPM Count (Ages 5-17)`                      REAL       null,\n    `Percent (%) Eligible FRPM (Ages 5-17)`       REAL       null,\n    `2013-14 CALPADS Fall 1 Certification Status` INTEGER    null,\n    foreign key (CDSCode) references schools (CDSCode)\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE satscores\n(\n    cds         TEXT not null\n        primary key,\n    rtype       TEXT  not null,\n    sname       TEXT null,\n    dname       TEXT null,\n    cname       TEXT null,\n    enroll12    INTEGER         not null,\n    NumTstTakr  INTEGER          not null,\n    AvgScrRead  INTEGER          null,\n    AvgScrMath  INTEGER          null,\n    AvgScrWrite INTEGER          null,\n    NumGE1500   INTEGER          null,\n    foreign key (cds) references schools (CDSCode)\n)\n\nCREATE TABLE schools\n(\n    CDSCode     TEXT not null\n        primary key,\n    NCESDist    TEXT  null,\n    NCESSchool  TEXT  null,\n    StatusType  TEXT  not null,\n    County      TEXT not null,\n    District    TEXT not null,\n    School      TEXT null,\n    Street      TEXT null,\n    StreetAbr   TEXT null,\n    City        TEXT null,\n    Zip         TEXT null,\n    State       TEXT  null,\n    MailStreet  TEXT null,\n    MailStrAbr  TEXT null,\n    MailCity    TEXT null,\n    MailZip     TEXT null,\n    MailState   TEXT  null,\n    Phone       TEXT null,\n    Ext         TEXT  null,\n    Website     TEXT null,\n    OpenDate    DATE        null,\n    ClosedDate  DATE        null,\n    Charter     INTEGER    null,\n    CharterNum  TEXT  null,\n    FundingType TEXT null,\n    DOC         TEXT  not null,\n    DOCType     TEXT not null,\n    SOC         TEXT  null,\n    SOCType     TEXT null,\n    EdOpsCode   TEXT  null,\n    EdOpsName   TEXT null,\n    EILCode     TEXT  null,\n    EILName     TEXT null,\n    GSoffered   TEXT null,\n    GSserved    TEXT  null,\n    Virtual     TEXT  null,\n    Magnet      INTEGER   null,\n    Latitude    REAL      null,\n    Longitude   REAL      null,\n    AdmFName1   TEXT null,\n    AdmLName1   TEXT null,\n    AdmEmail1   TEXT null,\n    AdmFName2   TEXT null,\n    AdmLName2   TEXT null,\n    AdmEmail2   TEXT null,\n    AdmFName3   TEXT  null,\n    AdmLName3   TEXT null,\n    AdmEmail3   TEXT null,\n    LastUpdate  DATE        not null\n)", "db_id": "california_schools", "difficulty": "challenging", "clusters": [{"cluster_id": "0", "vote_count": 1, "representative_sql": "SELECT s.AdmFName1, s.AdmLName1, s.AdmFName2, s.AdmLName2, s.AdmFName3, s.AdmLName3 FROM schools AS s INNER JOIN satscores AS ss ON s.CDSCode = ss.cds WHERE ss.NumGE1500 > 0 ORDER BY ss.NumGE1500 DESC NULLS FIRST LIMIT 1", "labels": {"output_semantics": "C", "constraint_semantics": "S", "ranking_semantics": "U", "relation_semantics": "S", "overall": "C"}, "reasons": {"output_semantics": "The SQL returns the first three administrative names (AdmFName1, AdmLName1, AdmFName2, AdmLName2, AdmFName3, AdmLName3) of the school with the highest number of test takers with SAT scores ≥ 1500. However, the question asks for 'his or her full name', which implies a single full name (first name and last name), not multiple names. The SQL returns multiple names, which contradicts the requirement.", "constraint_semantics": "The SQL correctly joins the `schools` and `satscores` tables on `CDSCode`, filters for `NumGE1500 > 0`, and selects the administrative names. It uses the correct column names and table names.", "ranking_semantics": "The SQL orders by `ss.NumGE1500` in descending order and uses `NULLS FIRST`, which is appropriate for ranking. However, the `LIMIT 1` is not explicitly required for the question, so this is not a material issue.", "relation_semantics": "The SQL correctly joins the `schools` and `satscores` tables on `CDSCode`, which is the appropriate relational join for the task.", "overall": "The SQL returns multiple administrative names, which contradicts the requirement to indicate 'his or her full name' (a single first and last name). The SQL also does not correctly handle the requirement to return the full name, which is not a single name but a combination of first and last names."}, "reason": "The SQL returns multiple administrative names, which contradicts the requirement to indicate 'his or her full name' (a single first and last name). The SQL also does not correctly handle the requirement to return the full name, which is not a single name but a combination of first and last names.", "verification": {"status": "ok", "cache_key": "75ba87afa14dcfad0bb5fb0051b66e508c45e5326be45b3d08185467419ff841", "attempts": 1, "prompt_version": "qrank-svem-semantic-v1", "backend": "transformers", "model": "Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B"}, "metadata": {"candidate_indices": [0]}}, {"cluster_id": "2", "vote_count": 2, "representative_sql": "SELECT T1.AdmFName1, T1.AdmLName1 FROM schools AS T1 INNER JOIN satscores AS T2 ON T1.CDSCode = T2.cds WHERE T2.NumGE1500 >= 1500 ORDER BY T2.NumGE1500 DESC LIMIT 1", "labels": {"output_semantics": "S", "constraint_semantics": "S", "ranking_semantics": "U", "relation_semantics": "S", "overall": "S"}, "reasons": {"output_semantics": "The SQL returns the full name (AdmFName1, AdmLName1) of the administrator, which matches the question's requirement. It filters schools with NumGE1500 >= 1500 and selects the highest number of test takers, then returns the first administrator (as per LIMIT 1).", "constraint_semantics": "The SQL uses the correct tables (schools and satscores), joins on CDSCode, and applies the correct filter (NumGE1500 >= 1500). It correctly returns the full name of the administrator.", "ranking_semantics": "The task does not require ranking, ordering, or limiting, so this is not applicable.", "relation_semantics": "The SQL correctly joins schools and satscores on CDSCode and filters by NumGE1500, which is appropriate for the task.", "overall": "The SQL satisfies the task by returning the correct administrator's full name for the school with the highest number of test takers with SAT scores >= 1500."}, "reason": "The SQL satisfies the task by returning the correct administrator's full name for the school with the highest number of test takers with SAT scores >= 1500.", "verification": {"status": "ok", "cache_key": "d249482b71a4739a092bf0959fe4701fad16a64bcc9c9e99c79a1b6ff9900e9c", "attempts": 1, "prompt_version": "qrank-svem-semantic-v1", "backend": "transformers", "model": "Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B"}, "metadata": {"candidate_indices": [2, 3]}}, {"cluster_id": "4", "vote_count": 1, "representative_sql": "WITH TopSchoolCTE AS (SELECT s.CDSCode, s.School, ss.NumGE1500, CASE WHEN NOT s.AdmFName1 IS NULL AND NOT s.AdmLName1 IS NULL THEN s.AdmFName1 || ' ' || s.AdmLName1 ELSE NULL END AS Admin1, CASE WHEN NOT s.AdmFName2 IS NULL AND NOT s.AdmLName2 IS NULL THEN s.AdmFName2 || ' ' || s.AdmLName2 ELSE NULL END AS Admin2, CASE WHEN NOT s.AdmFName3 IS NULL AND NOT s.AdmLName3 IS NULL THEN s.AdmFName3 || ' ' || s.AdmLName3 ELSE NULL END AS Admin3 FROM schools AS s INNER JOIN satscores AS ss ON s.CDSCode = ss.cds WHERE ss.NumGE1500 > 0 ORDER BY ss.NumGE1500 DESC NULLS FIRST LIMIT 1) SELECT Admin1, Admin2, Admin3 FROM TopSchoolCTE", "labels": {"output_semantics": "C", "constraint_semantics": "S", "ranking_semantics": "S", "relation_semantics": "S", "overall": "C"}, "reasons": {"output_semantics": "The SQL returns Admin1, Admin2, and Admin3 columns, but the question asks for 'his or her full name' (i.e., a single full name, not multiple).", "constraint_semantics": "The SQL correctly filters schools with NumGE1500 > 0, joins with satscores, and selects the top school by NumGE1500. It uses the correct columns (Admin1, Admin2, Admin3) and handles NULLs appropriately.", "ranking_semantics": "The SQL orders by NumGE1500 in descending order and limits to 1, which correctly identifies the school with the highest number of test takers with SAT scores >= 1500.", "relation_semant